caf", "targetName": "The Night Café", "context": "Modern Art movements transmit the themes of alienation and existentialism depicted in The Night Café, shaping contemporary artistic discourse."}], "places": [{"name": "Arles, France", "role": "Creation Site"}, {"name": "Paris, France", "role": "Artistic Hub"}, {"name": "Amsterdam, Netherlands", "role": "Cultural Influence"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: The Night Café", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "the-night-café"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q674846", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Night_Caf%C3%A9"], "tags": ["painting", "Paintings & Visual Art", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "The Night Café contributed to the historical record of the Modern period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to artistic heritage and cultural identity. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The Night Café significantly shaped the exploration of psychological themes in modern art, influencing future movements such as Expressionism and Surrealism. Its enduring legacy is reflected in ongoing discussions about mental health and the role of visual art in addressing complex human emotions.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-07T05:55:38Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28844797158", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Painting by vincent van gogh (yale university art gallery) Created by Vincent van Gogh. Created c. 1888.", "newValue": "The Night Café, painted by Vincent van Gogh in September 1888, stands as a testament to the emotional intensity and innovative spirit of the Post-Impressionist movement. Created in Arles, France, this work is noteworthy for its striking use of color and light, showcasing van Gogh's fascination with the effects of artificial illumination on everyday scenes. The painting depicts the interior of a café, where the psychological exploration of loneliness and existential despair is palpable, making it a significant contribution to the narrative of modern art and the human experience.

In creating The Night Café, van Gogh employed vivid colors, particularly greens and reds, to evoke a sense of unease and disquiet. This piece is notable for its portrayal of a space that is both inviting and alienating, a microcosm of urban life in the late 19th century. The café, frequented by various patrons at night, symbolizes the burgeoning café culture in Europe, serving as a social hub and a reflection of the changing dynamics of community life during this period. Van Gogh's letters to his brother Theo reveal his intent to convey the emotional weight of the scene, emphasizing the contrast between the vibrant colors and the dark undertones of the human condition.

The legacy of The Night Café extends beyond its immediate aesthetic impact; it has influenced generations of artists and scholars alike. Its representation of psychological depth within a seemingly mundane setting can be seen as a precursor to later modernist explorations of alienation and subjectivity. The painting continues to resonate in contemporary discussions about mental health and the role of art in expressing complex emotional states. Art historian Michael Fried noted, 'Van Gogh's work invites us to confront our own existential dilemmas, making his art timeless and universally relevant.'"}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-07T05:55:38Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28844797158", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Artistic patronage and creative expression"], "newValue": ["The rise of the Post-Impressionist movement in France influenced van Gogh's stylistic choices.", "The burgeoning café culture in late 19th century Europe provided a vibrant backdrop for social interaction and artistic expression.", "Van Gogh's personal struggles with mental health and isolation shaped the emotional intensity of his work."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-07T05:55:38Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28844797158", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to artistic heritage and cultural identity"], "newValue": ["The Night Café contributed to the understanding of color theory and emotional expression in art.", "It has inspired numerous artists and movements, including Expressionism and Surrealism, emphasizing psychological depth.", "The painting has become a cultural touchstone in discussions of mental health within the context of art."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-07T05:55:38Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28844797158", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "the-night-caf", "sourceName": "The Night Café", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "era-modern", "targetName": "Modern", "context": "The Night Café is situated with